Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayObjectQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e8c073b5-510e-3541-9be2-0e9b856c4a9e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid array object"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4caec69b-7c4e-de4c-a08e-0f4415edfde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Dimensions and Normal work directly on an array object, and further \
properties are read as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"arr", "[", "\"\<prop\>\"", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9da9eaf4-fb54-a947-99c8-672391997d35"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8317449a-b3b4-1b49-84a3-37fc12d3f005"],

Cell["Special arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cf9b2e75-ee78-c941-a140-b800eef24de4"],

Cell["\<\
Constant arrays and the generalized Kronecker deltas, in any order, dimension \
and value domain. Each declares the strongest symmetry that actually holds of \
it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90138ac5-ea9d-b349-b2e0-37ef37f72381"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ZeroArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "492b1d6d-b9b5-1541-84eb-1cc2941d75ee"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry zero"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0961bed4-7af8-be4f-b057-50200f934a4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["OneArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "36e3598c-94c9-7048-8b95-53f247b75db1"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "every entry one"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35a39899-71bd-1041-8a68-1e84a68bd6f4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["IdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f19bf871-8857-2d48-8e5d-715208f9453c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where all the indices agree, zero elsewhere"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab65d8d3-1eac-fe48-88cf-18563f8d5618"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["PartialIdentityArray", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c4f292a5-ba98-c645-808c-55ec52a17376"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one where the indices at chosen positions agree"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cf6f2da0-0360-5d42-92ec-7cc79c245f16"],

Cell["Contraction", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"55753610-f0aa-6544-b1d5-e61de7fba294"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayMultiply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "34f2d32e-408a-1e48-9cee-d71a6922678e"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "contract arrays by an index specification, in the manner of Einstein \
summation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f30a5557-6d74-6541-9a9d-350310870464"],

Cell["\<\
The specification is written either as a string, \"ij,jk->ik\", or as a rule \
between lists of index labels. An index may occur in any number of the arrays \
and in the output as well, so diagonals and three-way contractions are \
expressible, not only pairwise ones. A 0-array is named by an empty group of \
labels, and contracting every index away gives one back.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"596285eb-cedd-9b4f-99f2-b1b1f453cf7f"],

Cell["Drawing arrays", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9e0d5f47-b3dc-b943-93b7-cd7c05448842"],

Cell["\<\
There are two families, and an array of any order may be drawn in either. The \
flat family gives plane pictures throughout: a row of cells at order one, a \
grid at order two, and above that a nesting of those, a grid whose cells hold \
grids. The spatial family gives cubes arranged in space throughout: a line of \
cubes, a plane of them, a lattice, and above that the same lattices tiled \
through space, block beside block, all in one picture.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f2ca7868-f8e0-404d-870f-68d8cf35eb20"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Which indices go outside and which inside is a choice rather than a fact \
about the array, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Nesting\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d9d03921-0042-0d4c-a517-0322b872ae76"],
 " makes it. A flat picture holds one or two indices at a time and a spatial \
one holds three, so that is the only difference between the two defaults."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a77068af-c434-104f-aafe-06c527574500"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f43eda6f-bc14-354d-baef-6a60d730f781"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"543f9a25-6a1b-1147-a2da-08bcf123c8c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e1b26608-b81e-144e-81c4-789c857b83a5"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw an array of any order as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e85bbc7-88c6-1e49-8c2b-357a43e35394"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayNesting", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f9fa8c8f-0f5a-da4f-ac63-b031aa8f9a22"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "how the indices are split by default, for either family"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6e1cad6-b354-fd4d-b9e5-3bfe07ff9757"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a05c18a5-239d-9441-9aae-f489df844751"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "draw every array of a hypermatrix, in the plane"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c6810d54-919c-5e4a-9920-b2436a7727e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixGraphics3D", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c90dd884-a534-c345-b165-828813e7c557"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, as cubes in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c0717a0b-21cc-3f40-8b43-b9fb18b0dc3f"],

Cell["Adding and multiplying entry by entry", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"013953e5-d5e2-2847-ac93-edcdff059199"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayAdd", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c294d404-9174-0144-a408-55a14370b9f2"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "add arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b6ecdc0a-18c6-4149-b6b7-d5db43b6c1e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["ArrayTimes", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "eea2a9dc-7b3e-924f-80f6-e20e277ca69f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "multiply arrays entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c2079f3-1a31-e949-a5ad-901c408a2a7a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "These are the multilinear structure of arrays, as against the contraction \
ArrayMultiply. Arrays of the same dimensions combine entry by entry, and a \
0-array, having no shape of its own, reaches every entry \[LongDash] which is \
why scalar multiplication needs no name of its own. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Plus", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ad1b6701-87e3-8448-bdf5-68063e6de88d"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Times", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6e5cbd65-558b-604a-8b0b-8c9364a0ed3f"],
 " on array objects are the same operations, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", " ", "a"}], " ", "+", " ", "b"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4d3b37f9-72cb-bd44-baf2-ce9b6c385436"],
 " means what it looks like."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a71648de-dbd2-f64c-a6c7-a29cd2d1a927"],

Cell["Equational identities", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c14cfaaa-4a1f-ad41-b5eb-1df0b9ff1ff3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["FindArrayEquations", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a7658c81-07cf-1642-8516-e71c1b112c39"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "search for equations between all nestings of given operations over given \
arguments"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e2e54a5-afa2-ca44-be71-d4e19c9b7202"],

Cell["\<\
The search screens candidates on random numerical arrays first, which is \
fast, and verifies only the survivors on symbolic arrays. Matrix \
multiplication on three arguments returns associativity; the Fish product on \
five returns a twisted ternary associativity; the Bhattacharya-Mesner product \
on five returns nothing. An operation of arity one may be nested, so that the \
involutivity of a transpose is within reach, and an equation that follows \
from the others is not reported.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"517edb00-bffd-b54e-a98c-c4558cc00a1c"],

Cell["From hypergraphs to hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"61f9c8f9-c945-804f-abd2-e0a820cc3f37"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two halves of the package meet here. An edge has an arity and a \
symmetry type; an array has an order and a symmetry; and the two vocabularies \
line up one for one \[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Directed\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f1c3ec1b-2b5e-824f-ad6c-d35520873676"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Rigid\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "28d81e96-f6ca-8943-817a-88be62a13d12"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "87873925-bd09-3741-a451-ba2623a5d5fa"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Cyclic\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "176a049a-282c-9a4a-abaf-7a0e3676fc48"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Unordered\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e165c7ad-6ffe-f048-9130-6b284ec3c73d"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\"\<Symmetric\>\"", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"b98f4c73-3f6c-e74a-873e-c3458417e094"],
 ". An array holds one symmetry and one order, so the edges are gathered by \
arity and symmetry type together and each group becomes one array."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"767228fc-ff03-cb49-a22e-cdde823c4b43"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["AdjacencyHypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ebf4599c-a3a1-6d45-86f5-cc8c0400a7b0"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the adjacency hypermatrix of a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"178bad75-4589-9c4a-bd57-f1775f51873d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Identical copies of an edge share an entry, so a repeated edge comes out as \
an integer multiple. With ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Labeled\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4dcedf43-0774-a54b-8caf-a414f0875cbb"],
 " the entries are the edge labels themselves rather than counts, which needs \
the hypergraph to be simple \[LongDash] one entry cannot hold two labels."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8cfc7258-fc64-8642-8fb2-eb820c9e2188"],

Cell["\<\
The entry at an index tuple counts the edges sitting on it, and every tuple \
of an orbit reads the same count, which is what makes each array carry its \
symmetry by construction. Nothing is lost in the passage: the canonical \
entries name exactly the edges that went in.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0c9df9dc-2778-7447-ae9f-cc0ae5bbb5fe"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The vertices are a set, so numbering the indices is a choice; the \
Hypergraph constructor makes it by storing its vertices sorted. That is \
deterministic but not invariant \[LongDash] renaming the vertices can permute \
the indices \[LongDash] so for an invariant of the isomorphism class, compose \
with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["CanonicalHypergraph", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2232e8f9-2063-6c40-8aef-3a68592c5602"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0e6ac02a-65c8-8d40-a50e-641af11d758c"],

Cell["Hypermatrices", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"cf328b4b-8b6b-9c4b-bb5c-ff7fbe6e3a0b"],

Cell["\<\
A hypermatrix is a list of arrays held in canonical order: lowest order \
first, then the shorter dimensions, then symmetry taking symmetric before \
cyclic before rigid. Giving the same arrays in a different order produces the \
identical expression.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b1a3348-5475-1a46-904d-b40438124211"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Hypermatrix", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "064b3464-b432-d646-a544-09f999287c01"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a canonically ordered list of arrays"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"75ab8c0a-da27-dc40-9cec-3844d404fe78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixArrays", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d5fb1ef8-f05f-0549-acb9-65e57f50df9f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays, in canonical order"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"949fdf79-cdc2-e749-a656-d4c2df304349"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypermatrixQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f53f899a-3163-564c-96ab-972a52c4a53d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid hypermatrix object"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6ce1a917-b3f3-3d45-826f-b09785a5d0f5"],

Cell["Messages", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3aaabb63-5031-7e49-ad8d-7f658e239033"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "sym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"682c0514-15c5-b94b-afbe-a04003dd5680"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given edge symmetry type is not one of the three recognized ones"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"38f0c730-5ff3-974d-877d-e12d5da0f5d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Edge", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fe7739df-4954-b642-83f2-b30e30ba054a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hyperedge specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd02bb9e-56ac-4a49-989f-9d04261de6f0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "spec"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"043c7b41-411c-ac4c-adc5-b34be6353c87"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the expression is not a valid hypergraph specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d16c2fa0-864c-7d41-bf89-573e04a03d6c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypergraph", "::", "vlbl"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f8ea0ef8-218e-3947-aeb9-7629353158da"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one vertex identifier was given more than one label"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36c04f41-5244-f242-9eff-04d178050322"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"CanonicalHypergraph", "::", "large"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"f351756a-bbaa-9e4b-b56f-73bcbcebbbe3"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the isomorphism search will be slow at this size"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f3971e3e-404f-ae4d-b935-23a6b4968854"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "nosym"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e2145da8-c201-5c42-a551-648f62018851"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not invariant under the declared symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7867aa55-4d12-d346-8e85-6f40a43f5865"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "irreg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"ed68f806-4f8d-6a4b-a42e-94e9f324ed36"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an irregular array cannot carry a symmetry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ec045217-a6a5-d940-969c-9fa31224dc99"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayObject", "::", "data"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"502f1d0d-1cec-da48-82f7-39facbbd7b48"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the entries are not a rectangular array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c5e01cb7-b9f6-fa4b-aa32-f8fbb4b1a54c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"GenerateSymbolicArray", "::", "name"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cd901f46-a99d-324f-a999-c8c40c89279a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array name must be a symbol or a string"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fdff99b0-5392-444a-ba8c-c3f8bb78613d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"Hypermatrix", "::", "arrays"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"123ebd97-bf0d-534d-91c6-342c8bc7a7e5"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "something given was not an array"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8e37c919-ff65-374b-b383-23a0e2beb432"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "rank"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5220f066-3690-2841-a347-51e2fe3c1999"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an array has a different number of indices from its specification"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a76367d6-57cb-a44b-a31e-e0ef110be320"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f2acb3e4-c5ac-2f48-903c-790ac421f267"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "one index label is used with two different lengths"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cf5893a-6eab-0249-b80b-6cea8cb7917d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayMultiply", "::", "out"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"e0384840-a718-7e46-a922-1f9fbca12766"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "an output index does not occur among the inputs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b45253d-967d-4b48-8b02-1ee30876a0e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "arity"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2622a35c-26bb-1841-bebf-b65531e8e36f"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arity of an operation could not be determined"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4c4ce519-0189-9d4e-8642-78762f5fa4a3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "eval"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"29c84283-36f3-bd4c-bad5-9ae2fc52d484"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no nesting evaluated on arrays of the shape used"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"24a4737f-c7f7-ec4f-b34a-95808b676d8b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "shape"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"74565de2-8241-cd49-b53d-e21785d3203a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "no order from 1 to 5 suits every operation"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"825c03c5-9247-4047-b3be-8c1d7cda9e21"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"FindArrayEquations", "::", "depth"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2c2b9d0b-3d0f-1643-95bf-4726b9fa5c73"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "\"UnaryDepth\" is not a non-negative integer"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"32981474-b72b-c148-8dd5-6dd693be8f24"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayAdd", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8d9c1428-d22d-2941-9119-3e8aa7ccb420"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the arrays are not of the same dimensions"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7431b5bb-00d2-d94b-8120-8a8a37d1df6f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayTimes", "::", "dims"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8038d0da-2630-3e4b-8c21-b3eff593bc2d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the same, for multiplication entry by entry"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bc326a54-9cd1-614f-9ebc-e845d55b0678"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "nesting"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"ac13ecd5-af5f-9946-b6a1-723b135d398d"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the given nesting does not account for every index"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a8159328-a1a6-194a-94a9-d91c4a198c59"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"3dc32d1f-785f-af47-81c5-e4855834b1f3"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than two indices has no flat picture"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8f6ed522-14c6-094a-ae27-7ae9b08ce68b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics3D", "::", "block"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"46e95bba-3990-6141-9583-556f2994eff7"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a block of more than three indices has nowhere to go in space"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2b43246-9d28-2e45-8a9f-34700dbf9446"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5a41e58a-ad67-1544-acbe-783055f529e5"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the argument is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ee60bd5-2998-044f-a7e5-51e8d60d602a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "::", "hg"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"04704561-5cb6-d641-b7e6-47d4b27038be"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a side of a rule is not a hypergraph"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a2e9decd-0bc7-b24c-a989-1a28ff91ed0b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRuleApply", "::", "rule"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4a033be1-9bf5-8f4f-bd67-08a10c00f70a"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "what was given is not a rewrite rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"be08e8ed-5945-9843-b357-857e74de898c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"AdjacencyHypermatrix", "::", "nonsimple"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9030b047-6362-9f48-80ff-021db578e301"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "labels cannot be entries unless no edge is repeated"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"42d5b368-57d1-204a-9375-8867a884380e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayGraphics", "::", "big"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"7f47f498-a1d7-8345-9a4a-ff5f951b2088"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the array has too many entries to be drawn legibly"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"03f2c0aa-a071-1848-b0e2-9b31412b26da"],

Cell["Rewriting", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"84d050bf-1e50-b946-a8cf-4488d4d60220"],

Cell["\<\
A rewrite rule is a pair of hypergraphs. Applying it means finding the ways \
its input sits inside a hypergraph, and for each of them replacing what was \
matched by the output. Each such way is an event, reported as an association \
saying not only what the new hypergraph is but what was matched, what was \
created and what was destroyed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12b7869a-256c-bd47-9099-d3ea2816d62b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRule", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "09b01861-eee2-9846-a34e-78a8ad269543"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "a rewrite rule, as a pair of hypergraphs"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fe8f86a-f33e-7a48-afaf-6a70a271e278"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleQ", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8d12f8b7-5d45-5f4f-9900-cf2f5c8823e9"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "test for a valid rule"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cac230e3-95e8-9446-9548-15d094c47192"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"da8cc0ee-19ec-1347-8ddc-436b743d942c"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "apply a rule, giving one event per match; rule[hg] is the same"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35467e5c-10a3-9b42-82fc-c1b53afef27b"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleMatches", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5c24b155-4b6c-374b-a9a1-4244cfb04557"],
 " \[LongDash] ",
 "the ways the input sits inside a hypergraph, without rewriting"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ca8a3fe8-8c10-d641-961d-370e2e11e6ab"],

Cell["\<\
Symmetry types must agree between a pattern edge and the edge it lies on, and \
the pattern is matched over the orderings that symmetry allows.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"98f8bd1b-3aba-d942-949a-6e908ea77f16"],

Cell["\<\
A label on a rule's input is read three ways. A bare symbol is a variable: it \
matches whatever label it is laid against and remembers it, and the output's \
labels are expressions in those variables, written out with the bindings put \
in \[LongDash] which is how a pair of composable edges labelled x and y \
becomes one labelled for their composite. No label at all is a wildcard. \
Anything else is a literal. Vertex labels bind the same way as edge labels, \
so a rule whose whole input is a single labelled vertex can name what it \
creates after it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c1512673-a140-544b-b6d9-12c6880cf895"],

Cell["\<\
The shape of all this follows the reference paclet, so that rules written for \
that one read the same here, including the label-variable rules of its \
chemoid notebooks.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e6b81934-9f44-9045-a746-88eb126888b4"],

Cell["Not yet implemented", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"944b83ba-3fb2-0544-9b46-cf899e35ec0c"],

Cell["\<\
The objects, isomorphism, the array algebra, the drawing, the adjacency \
hypermatrix and the core of rewriting are all in place. What remains of the \
rewriting is the machinery around it: the generations of states a rule \
produces, the causal graph of its events, and the conditions under which two \
events depend on one another or their matches overlap. After that come the \
plex diagrams that tie rewriting to hypermatrix algebra, and a visual editor \
for hypergraphs and for rules.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e7466631-66fb-4d46-aa92-d896cb3d1f68"]
},
WindowSize->{820, 750},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Microsoft Windows (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"eb30a193-e9eb-c84f-adad-77ff08f93a51"
]
